# Sidebar

:notation:
  \eig $\lambda$ eigenvalue
::

## Introduction
  {:label: sec-intro}

We :write: $\eig$ for the spectral radius :: of the matrix throughout.

## Results
  {:label: sec-results}

:theorem: {:label: thm-x} A claim about $\eig$.::

:proof:
  :step: :assume: $\eig$ is the spectral radius of :ref:thm-x::.::
  :step: {:label: st-1} First, $\eig$ is real.::
  :step: {:label: st-2} Then it is bounded, by :ref:st-1::.::
  :step: :qed: Done by :ref:st-2::.::
::

As :ref:thm-x:: shows, the claim holds.
